{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "footprint_stroke_source_research",
  "profile": "kicad9-pcb-editor-default-strokes-v1",
  "conclusions": [
    "KiCad9 EDA_SHAPE DEFAULT resolves to SOLID. All four previous GRAPHIC_STROKE_UNSUPPORTED files in the 120-file sample use DEFAULT, not dash/dot.",
    "PCB editor default ratios 12/3 with round-cap correction 1 imply centreline dash=11w, dot=.2w, gap=4w. This fixed profile cannot recover project/render settings from .kicad_mod.",
    "Each rectangle/polygon straight edge is a separate shape; phase restarts at its source start. Last marks clip to the endpoint.",
    "FreePCB2 2.428 outlines store width/visibility/hatch/layer and corners, with no native dash style. Separate straight outlines require a loss for editable style/render settings and unvalidated caps/joins.",
    "Inclusive KiCad ClipLine can produce zero-length endpoint point-marks. This restricted profile emits only positive-length marks; isolated endpoint caps are explicitly omitted with loss in diagnostics and JSON."
  ],
